[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
REVYTECH Ly is installed and auto-configured on package install:

  - /etc/gettytab  → Ly entry (lo=/usr/local/bin/ly_wrapper)
  - /etc/ttys      → ttyv1 uses getty Ly
  - seatd_enable=YES
  - /usr/local/etc/ly/config.ini (from sample if missing)

Original /etc files are preserved once as:
  /etc/gettytab.orig.revytech-ly
  /etc/ttys.orig.revytech-ly
Each later edit also writes a timestamped /etc/*.bak.revytech-ly.<stamp>.

Re-run anytime:  doas /usr/local/sbin/revytech-ly-enable
Restore/manual:  compare against the .orig.revytech-ly copies

Reboot to use Ly on ttyv1.
Wayfire session: /usr/local/etc/ly/custom-sessions/wayfire.desktop
EOM
}
{ type: upgrade
  message: <<EOM
Package upgrade re-applies FreeBSD getty/ttys integration (with backups).
Review /usr/local/etc/ly/config.ini against config.ini.sample if needed.
EOM
}
{ type: remove
  message: <<EOM
On deinstall, revytech-ly restores /etc/gettytab and /etc/ttys from
*.orig.revytech-ly when those snapshots exist. Timestamped .bak files
are left for forensics.
EOM
}
]
